Package: rhodep-gpu-vulkan
Version: 2
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: rhodep port
Depends: mesa-vulkan-drivers, libvulkan1, vulkan-tools
Recommends: vulkan-validationlayers
Description: Vulkan on the Adreno 619 via Turnip (freedreno) for Motorola rhodep
 Mesa ships Turnip, the open Vulkan driver for Adreno, inside
 mesa-vulkan-drivers, but two things stop it being picked up on this port out of
 the box. The loader has to find the freedreno ICD manifest, and on a device
 with no other Vulkan implementation `vulkaninfo` otherwise reports zero
 devices; and the driver has to be pinned, because Turnip on the A619 is young
 and an unattended upgrade could regress it under the compositor.
 .
 This package points the Vulkan loader at Mesa's freedreno ICD
 (VK_ICD_FILENAMES / VK_DRIVER_FILES), holds mesa-vulkan-drivers to the
 validated version, and registers its files with the port's protection so an
 apt run or a stray editor cannot quietly undo it. Verified with `vulkaninfo`
 reporting "Turnip Adreno (TM) 619" and `vkcube` rendering.
 .
 Note: KWin already runs accelerated on this GPU through the freedreno GL
 driver; this adds the Vulkan path on top, which zink, dxvk/wine and native
 Vulkan applications use. GL is unaffected either way.
